<p>
  Hi, my name is Ryan Holt, the creative developer of Tome Keeper, a PDF reader for tabletop roleplaying games. As a
  TTRPG enthusiast who moves frequently, I’ve found it difficult to keep physical editions of these games, which is the
  preferred method for many. I searched for the “perfect” reader for my collection, but most readers came with
  excessive bloat.
</p>
<p>
  So I asked myself, could I redefine how a user experiences a TTRPG rulebook? Can I get close to the immersion of a
  physical book and the experience that gives us? Tome Keeper is my answer—an attempt to elevate how we collect, open,
  and experience our vast PDF libraries for the games we love.
</p>
